Edge Device
Your Vehicle Architecture (Typical for Autonomous Machines)

Based on what you described, the tractor probably has something like this:

Vehicle  

Sensors
 ├─ Cameras
 ├─ LiDAR
 ├─ GPS
 └─ IMU
        │
        ▼
NVIDIA Xavier (Autonomy Computer)
        │
        │  ROS / ROS2 Topics
        ▼
Intel NUC (Edge Gateway)
        │
        ├─ Python Device Agent (systemd)
        ├─ Telemetry service
        └─ MQTT client
        │
        ▼
AWS IoT Core
        │
        ▼
Cloud Backend

----------------------------------------                           
ROS → Cloud Telemetry Bridge

Your Python service probably acts as a ROS-to-MQTT bridge.

Example flow:

ROS Topic
   ↓
Python ROS node
   ↓
Convert message → JSON
   ↓
Publish MQTT
   ↓
AWS IoT Core       
-----------------------
Fleet Management Application (your cloud platform)
        │
        │ REST APIs / backend logic
        ▼
Device Management Layer
        │
        ├── OTA orchestration
        ├── Fleet database
        ├── Logs & telemetry
        └── Device commands
        │
        ▼
AWS IoT Core
        │
        ▼
Vehicle (NUC)

Python device agent
      │
      ├ Docker OTA
      ├ Telemetry
      ├ Command execution
      └ Log upload


--------------
